      ],
      "description": "A double-faced coat needs no lining, which is why it drapes the way it does. Two layers of Italian wool are woven as one cloth and then separated by hand along every edge, turned in and closed with a saddle stitch — around 14 metres of it in each coat. The result is a garment with the weight of an overcoat and the fluidity of a robe.\n\nWe cut it generously through the body so it sits over a jacket without pulling, with a natural shoulder that follows your own line rather than imposing a new one. Patch pockets are set low and deep enough for gloves.",
      "details": [
        "Double-faced 640gsm wool from a mill in Biella, Italy",
        "Fully unlined; all edges hand-turned and saddle-stitched",
        "Natural shoulder with no padding or canvas",
        "Horn buttons with hand-worked keyhole buttonholes",
        "Two low patch pockets and one interior chest pocket",
        "Centre back vent for movement when seated"
      ],
      "composition": "88% virgin wool, 12% cashmere. Horn buttons.",
      "care": [
        "Dry clean only, by a specialist",
        "Brush along the nap after wear",
        "Store on a broad wooden hanger",
        "Air rather than clean where possible"
      ],
      "fitNote": "Relaxed. Model is 6'1\" with a 39\" chest, wearing size M.",
      "origin": "Woven in Biella, Italy. Made in Porto, Portugal.",
      "releasedAt": "2026-07-02",
