      "description": "Most belts are two thin layers of split leather glued together — they crack along the fold within two years. This is a single 3.5mm strip of full-grain bridle leather from a tannery in Northampton, edge-bevelled, burnished and hand-finished with beeswax.\n\nThe buckle is solid cast brass on a stitched keeper, so it can be replaced rather than binning the belt.",
      "details": [
        "3.5mm full-grain English bridle leather, single ply",
        "Solid cast brass buckle on a stitched keeper",
        "Hand-bevelled and burnished edges, beeswax finish",
        "Five holes at 25mm centres",
        "35mm width — fits standard tailoring belt loops",
        "Buckle is replaceable; refinishing offered at cost"
      ],
      "composition": "100% full-grain bovine leather. Solid brass hardware.",
